THERMODYNAMIC RELATIONAL DERIVATIVE TREE 
Mapping all first-order derivatives into SID / PED / Q-mode

DERIVATIVE TREE (simplified connections)

                (∂P/∂V)_S
               /         \
              /           \
     -(∂P/∂S)_V               (∂S/∂V)_P
        |                         |
    Maxwell                   cyclic
        |                         |
     (∂T/∂V)_S                 (∂P/∂T)_S
     /         \               /         \
    /           \             /           \
-(∂T/∂S)_V   (∂S/∂V)_T   -(∂P/∂S)_T   (∂S/∂T)_P
    |             |           |             |
    |          Maxwell     Maxwell          |
    |             |           |             |
  T/C_v      (∂P/∂T)_V     (∂T/∂V)_P      C_p/T
                |             |
             cyclic         cyclic
                |             |
              -αV           1/(κV)   etc.

REDUCTIONS
T/C_v          temperature over heat capacity at constant volume
-αV            thermal expansion coefficient times volume
1/(κV)         isothermal compressibility (related to volume)
-κ/α           ratio of compressibility to thermal expansion
C_p/T          heat capacity at constant pressure over temperature

============================================================
RDG LAYERS AND TYPES
------------------------------------------------------------

SID  = State-Identity Domain
       Abstract state variables and their relational identities.
       Carrier: X ∈ {P, V, T, S}

PED  = Partial-Edge Domain
       Directed edges: constrained partial derivatives.
       Objects: D[X,Y|Z] := (∂X/∂Y)_Z

Q    = Quotient / Potential Domain
       Thermodynamic potentials as quotient charts of SID.
       Objects: U(S,V), H(S,P), F(T,V), G(T,P)

DERIVATIVE TREE (connections)
(∂P/∂V)_S
  ├─ Maxwell → −(∂P/∂S)_V → (∂T/∂V)_S → T/C_v
  └─ cyclic  → (∂S/∂V)_P → (∂P/∂T)_S → (∂S/∂T)_P → C_p/T
                └─ Maxwell → (∂P/∂T)_V → α/κ
                             └─ cyclic → (∂V/∂T)_P → α V
                                          (∂V/∂P)_T → −κ V

============================================================
SID: STATE VARIABLES AND TYPES
------------------------------------------------------------

SID = { P, V, T, S }

Type declarations:
    P : Pressure-type
    V : Volume-type
    T : Temperature-type
    S : Entropy-type

Each X ∈ SID is a scalar field on the underlying state manifold M.


============================================================
Q-MODE: THERMODYNAMIC POTENTIALS AS QUOTIENT CHARTS
------------------------------------------------------------

Potentials:
    U : M → R, natural chart (S,V)
    H : M → R, natural chart (S,P)
    F : M → R, natural chart (T,V)
    G : M → R, natural chart (T,P)

Differentials (Q-mode defining relations):
    dU = T dS − P dV
    dH = T dS + V dP
    dF = −S dT − P dV
    dG = −S dT + V dP

Role:
    Mixed second partials in these charts generate Maxwell edges in PED.


============================================================
PED: PARTIAL DERIVATIVE EDGES
------------------------------------------------------------

General PED object:
    D[X,Y|Z] := (∂X/∂Y)_Z

Domain:
    X,Y,Z ∈ SID, X ≠ Y, Z ≠ X,Y

Canonical first-order PED edges (16):
    D[P,V|T], D[P,V|S], D[P,T|V], D[P,T|S]
    D[V,P|T], D[V,P|S], D[V,T|P], D[V,T|S]
    D[T,V|S], D[T,V|P], D[T,P|S], D[T,P|V]
    D[S,V|T], D[S,V|P], D[S,P|T], D[S,P|V]


============================================================
MEASURABLE COEFFICIENTS AS TERMINAL PED MORPHISMS
------------------------------------------------------------

α   := (1/V) D[V,T|P] = (1/V) (∂V/∂T)_P
κ   := −(1/V) D[V,P|T] = −(1/V) (∂V/∂P)_T
C_p := T D[S,T|P] = T (∂S/∂T)_P
C_v := T D[S,T|V] = T (∂S/∂T)_V

These close derivative chains into experimentally accessible terminals.


============================================================
MAXWELL RELATIONS AS PED-SYMMETRY EDGES
------------------------------------------------------------

From Q-mode mixed second partials:

    D[T,V|S] = −D[P,S|V]
    D[T,P|S] =  D[V,S|P]
    D[S,V|T] =  D[P,T|V]
    D[S,P|T] = −D[V,T|P]

RDG form:
    Maxwell_U : D[T,V|S] + D[P,S|V] = 0
    Maxwell_H : D[T,P|S] − D[V,S|P] = 0
    Maxwell_F : D[S,V|T] − D[P,T|V] = 0
    Maxwell_G : D[S,P|T] + D[V,T|P] = 0


============================================================
CYCLIC RELATIONS AS PED-LOOP CONSTRAINTS
------------------------------------------------------------

For any triple (X,Y,Z) ∈ SID:

    D[X,Y|Z] · D[Y,Z|X] · D[Z,X|Y] = −1

RDG:
    Cyclic(X,Y,Z) : D[X,Y|Z] · D[Y,Z|X] · D[Z,X|Y] + 1 = 0

Examples:
    Cyclic(P,V,T) : D[P,V|T] · D[V,T|P] · D[T,P|V] + 1 = 0
    Cyclic(P,V,S) : D[P,V|S] · D[V,S|P] · D[S,P|V] + 1 = 0
    Cyclic(T,S,V) : D[T,S|V] · D[S,V|T] · D[V,T|S] + 1 = 0


============================================================
CANONICAL REDUCTIONS: PED → MEASURABLE TERMINALS
------------------------------------------------------------

1)  D[V,T|P] = α V
2)  D[V,P|T] = −κ V
3)  D[P,T|V] = α / κ
4)  D[S,V|T] = α / κ
5)  D[S,P|T] = −α V
6)  D[T,V|S] = −(T/C_v)(α/κ)
7)  D[P,V|S] = −(C_p/C_v)/(κ V)
8)  D[P,V|T] = −1/(κ V)
9)  D[V,T|S] = α V (C_p/C_v)
10) D[V,P|S] = −κ V (C_p/C_v)
11) D[P,T|S] = (α/κ)(C_p/C_v)
12) D[T,P|S] = (T α V)/C_p
13) D[T,V|P] = −(T α)/C_p
14) D[S,V|P] = −C_p/(T α V)
15) D[S,P|V] = −(α V C_v)/T
16) D[T,P|V] = (α V T)/C_v


============================================================
SUMMARY
------------------------------------------------------------

SID:
    Carrier: {P, V, T, S}

PED:
    Edges: D[X,Y|Z] with X,Y,Z ∈ SID, X ≠ Y, Z ≠ X,Y
    Constraints:
        Maxwell_U, Maxwell_H, Maxwell_F, Maxwell_G
        Cyclic(X,Y,Z) for all triples

Q-mode:
    Potentials: U(S,V), H(S,P), F(T,V), G(T,P)
    Role: Generate Maxwell symmetry edges in PED via mixed second partials

Terminal morphisms:
    α, κ, C_p, C_v, T, V

All 16 first-order PED edges reduce to these terminals,
closing the RDG triad SID / PED / Q into experimentally accessible form.
